================================================================================================
CIRCULANT INSTANCE: negation x -> -x is an involutive anti-automorphism (n odd)
================================================================================================
  n= 3: all    2 circulant tournaments: negation anti-auto OK ; order(negation)=2
  n= 5: all    4 circulant tournaments: negation anti-auto OK ; order(negation)=2
  n= 7: all    8 circulant tournaments: negation anti-auto OK ; order(negation)=2
  n= 9: all   16 circulant tournaments: negation anti-auto OK ; order(negation)=2
  n=11: all   32 circulant tournaments: negation anti-auto OK ; order(negation)=2
  n=13: all   64 circulant tournaments: negation anti-auto OK ; order(negation)=2

=> the dihedral group D_n = <rotation, negation> acts on every circulant
   tournament with rotations as automorphisms and reflections as
   anti-automorphisms; the reflection is involutive: circulants are always
   DIHEDRAL-split.  The staircase reflection sigma(v) = n+1-v plays the
   same role for grid-symmetric tilings (base-path dihedral).
DONE.
